Bada is a working Quick Share implementation for Android, written in Kotlin.
The Barq app consumes libbarq_protocol, which is a Rust port of the protocol layers of its core-protocol
module: the UKEY2 handshake, D2D key derivation, the SecureMessage envelope,
the Nearby Connections and Nearby Sharing wire formats, and the state machines
over them. The code is rewritten rather than copied -- the languages and the
process model differ -- but the protocol knowledge is theirs, and several
non-obvious constants in this implementation exist because Bada found them
first and wrote down why.

Where a field value or a byte layout was taken from Bada, the source comment
says so. See docs/CREDITS.md.

